  "preamble": "The Common Slavic back yer *ъ, a short high back vowel conventionally written *ŭ, was lost in weak position and vocalized in strong position. Bulgarian vocalized strong *ъ to the mid back unrounded vowel ъ [ɤ], the same vowel that continues *ǫ (Sussex & Cubberley 2006): *sъnъ > сън, *mъxъ > мъх. The front yer *ь gave e instead (ден, пес).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Yer Vocalization, Unrounding, Lowering",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Bulgarian",
      "languageFamily": "South Slavic",
      "examples": [
